OBSERVATIONS (not failures, for the backlog):
  O1. `json:"floor_monthly_real,omitempty"` makes a saved 0 indistinguishable from a legacy
      record with no field, so a 0 always falls back to the policy floor. Harmless today —
      the input is `required` with min="0.01" and normalizeSpendingRequest/OptimizeSpending
      reject floors < .01 — but it means the field can never record "explicitly zero", unlike
      its sibling MaxShortfallPct which deliberately has no omitempty for that reason.
  O2. The sibling guardrail-optimizer form (web/templates/components/whatif/guardrail_optimizer.html:6)
      still hardcodes value="7500" for its own floor_monthly_real input and has no saved-preference
      prefill. Different feature, untouched by RC1, out of scope — noted only because the two
      forms share the field NAME and a user may expect the same memory there.
  O3. TestSpendingApplyKeepsComparisonMinimum sets p.request and p.form to the same 7000, so it
      does not by itself pin the "raw form, not normalized request" contract stated in criterion 1;
      my PROBE A did. Promoting that probe (request 1234 / form 7000) into the shipped test would
      make the contract mutation-resistant against a future switch to p.request.
